          "date": "2026-10-09 12:53:31.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20917 dkms: find in-kernel RDMA headers in Debian",
        "message": "LU-20917 dkms: find in-kernel RDMA headers in Debian\n\nThe DKMS config detects in-kernel o2ib support by checking for\nrdma_cm.h, ib_cm.h and ib_verbs.h under\n${kernel_source_dir}/include/rdma.  On Debian, the kernel headers\nare split into an arch-specific package and a \"-common\" package,\nand the generic include/ tree (including include/rdma) lives only in\nthe latter, under /usr/src/linux-headers-<version>-common. Since the\narch-specific directory has no include/rdma, can_o2ib_in_kernel stays\n\"no\" and the in-kernel o2ib stack is never detected, so ko2iblnd is\nnot built.\n\n  modprobe: FATAL: Module ko2iblnd not found in directory\n  /lib/modules/<kernel-version>\n\nSearch both ${kernel_source_dir} and\n/usr/src/linux-headers-${kernelver%-*}-common for the RDMA headers,\nand set can_o2ib_in_kernel=yes as soon as a directory contains all\nthree.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manhong Dai <manhong.dai@netapp.com>\nSigned-off-by: Walker, Chris <chris.walker@netapp.com>\nChange-Id: I94ff1d23efc711db1b396d050dcf0fd5468d4c87\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
